00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:00:42,147 --> 00:00:46,068
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

2
00:00:53,492 --> 00:00:54,493
Here we go.

3
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,667
Try a little harder this time.

4
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,293
At this rate, I will win again.

5
00:01:03,377 --> 00:01:05,545
Please take it easy, Your Highness.

6
00:01:05,629 --> 00:01:07,339
We do not want a stray arrow to ruin

7
00:01:07,422 --> 00:01:08,799
all the beautiful peonies.

8
00:01:08,882 --> 00:01:11,093
-Do you find them beautiful as well?
-Yes.

9
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:14,262
I was right to clear the patch
and plant peonies.

10
00:01:14,346 --> 00:01:15,931
When it comes to flowers,

11
00:01:16,014 --> 00:01:19,184
they need big heads like this
to be worth looking at.

12
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:23,230
A peony, beaded with dewdrops
like pearls, was plucked…

13
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:26,692
by a beauty as she passed a window.

14
00:01:31,905 --> 00:01:33,699
With a smile, she asks her beloved,

15
00:01:34,199 --> 00:01:35,826
"Which is fairer, the flower or I?"

16
00:01:35,909 --> 00:01:37,994
The young lord answers
in gentle mischief.

17
00:01:39,162 --> 00:01:40,330
"The flower is far fairer."

18
00:01:40,414 --> 00:01:43,458
I, too, find the peonies
more beautiful than Your Majesty.

19
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,880
I can never win against you.

20
00:01:48,964 --> 00:01:52,342
No flower in the world could be
as beautiful as you.

21
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:54,511
Your Majesty.

22
00:01:54,594 --> 00:01:56,179
It is time for your midday meal.

23
00:01:56,263 --> 00:01:58,974
What brings you all the way to the Annex?

24
00:01:59,057 --> 00:02:00,183
I have

25
00:02:00,809 --> 00:02:02,978
a gift for you.

26
00:02:09,025 --> 00:02:11,153
Your Majesty, what is this?

27
00:02:11,236 --> 00:02:13,363
Your health seems
to have declined of late.

28
00:02:13,447 --> 00:02:17,117
I personally asked the Royal Infirmary
to concoct you a restorative tonic.

29
00:02:21,830 --> 00:02:23,165
A restorative tonic…

30
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,085
<i>Royal Consort Hui of the Kang clan</i>
<i>shall accept the poison.</i>

31
00:02:30,964 --> 00:02:33,383
Royal Consort Hui,
what is the meaning of this?

32
00:02:34,426 --> 00:02:37,763
Your Majesty, please take the tonic away.

33
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:39,681
I cannot stand

34
00:02:40,432 --> 00:02:42,517
even the smell of tonic.

35
00:03:10,378 --> 00:03:12,380
Hey, Ms. Shin Seo-ri.

36
00:03:13,173 --> 00:03:15,425
Ms. Shin Seo-ri, wake up.

37
00:03:15,509 --> 00:03:16,885
The shock must've been too much.

38
00:03:16,968 --> 00:03:18,220
I'll call an ambulance.

39
00:03:18,303 --> 00:03:20,639
No, this isn't
just another minor fender bender.

40
00:03:20,722 --> 00:03:21,932
The media may exploit this.

41
00:03:22,015 --> 00:03:23,642
-Call Dr. Kim.
-Yes, sir.

42
00:03:25,977 --> 00:03:26,853
Wait.

43
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:33,693
Ms. Shin, are you awake?

44
00:03:47,582 --> 00:03:50,669
EPISODE 2
A GUIDE TO OPTIMIZING YOUR FATE

45
00:03:57,342 --> 00:04:00,387
<i>Given that he resides</i>
<i>in such lofty chambers,</i>

46
00:04:00,470 --> 00:04:03,014
<i>he must be</i>
<i>at least a high-ranking minister.</i>

47
00:04:03,723 --> 00:04:05,183
<i>He has the pedigree, influence,</i>

48
00:04:05,267 --> 00:04:06,893
<i>and even that handsome face.</i>

49
00:04:06,977 --> 00:04:08,603
<i>He truly has it all.</i>

50
00:04:08,687 --> 00:04:09,855
How did you know

51
00:04:10,689 --> 00:04:12,482
a mannequin would fall from the sky?

52
00:04:12,566 --> 00:04:13,525
I just knew.

53
00:04:13,608 --> 00:04:16,319
My instincts in that sphere
are exceptionally keen.

54
00:04:25,787 --> 00:04:26,788
Damn it.

55
00:04:26,872 --> 00:04:28,290
Arrest that assassin at once!

56
00:04:37,299 --> 00:04:38,800
What are you waiting for?

57
00:04:38,884 --> 00:04:40,260
Seize her this instant!

58
00:04:45,891 --> 00:04:48,226
Take him into custody immediately!

59
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:50,312
<i>I am endowed</i>
<i>with a remarkably keen sixth sense.</i>

60
00:04:50,395 --> 00:04:52,522
It has allowed me to survive
countless attempts

61
00:04:52,606 --> 00:04:53,857
of poisoning and assassination.

62
00:04:54,858 --> 00:04:57,986
Thanks to me, you have preserved
your precious life.

63
00:05:00,488 --> 00:05:01,823
Don't tell me.

64
00:05:02,824 --> 00:05:04,242
Were you in on it?

65
00:05:06,995 --> 00:05:09,331
Are you implying I am involved
with those schemers

66
00:05:09,414 --> 00:05:11,416
who lower themselves to using assassins?

67
00:05:12,208 --> 00:05:13,501
I never scheme from the shadows.

68
00:05:13,585 --> 00:05:15,462
I strike necks openly.

69
00:05:15,545 --> 00:05:18,006
So you're not one of them,
but you just happened to pass out

70
00:05:18,089 --> 00:05:20,175
in front of my car <i>and</i> save me today?

71
00:05:20,258 --> 00:05:21,801
I think I get the gist of it.

72
00:05:21,885 --> 00:05:25,263
I'll have Mr. Son compensate you
for your troubles. You may leave now.

73
00:05:26,222 --> 00:05:27,766
Now, hold on.

74
00:05:28,433 --> 00:05:31,436
Do you take me for some beggar,
groveling for scraps?

75
00:05:33,521 --> 00:05:35,649
You are not as perceptive as you appear.

76
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:38,652
I have something
that you desperately need.

77
00:05:38,735 --> 00:05:42,447
Hence, I was going to give you
the chance to make a deal with me.

78
00:05:45,617 --> 00:05:47,327
You want to make a deal with me?

79
00:05:47,410 --> 00:05:50,705
Even with all these subordinates
at your feet, your life hangs by a thread.

80
00:05:50,789 --> 00:05:53,500
What use are absolute power
and worldly riches?

81
00:05:53,583 --> 00:05:54,834
Before a fleeting life,

82
00:05:55,418 --> 00:05:57,963
even the supreme sovereign's throne
is but vanity.

83
00:06:00,966 --> 00:06:02,050
I shall safeguard

84
00:06:02,550 --> 00:06:05,011
the flickering flame you call your life.

85
00:06:06,012 --> 00:06:07,389
Keep me by your side.

86
00:06:11,935 --> 00:06:13,228
Unhand me at once!

87
00:06:13,311 --> 00:06:14,813
Do you know who I am?

88
00:06:17,065 --> 00:06:18,400
Unhand me!

89
00:06:19,234 --> 00:06:20,485
Damn it.

90
00:06:20,568 --> 00:06:22,696
How can you be
such a poor judge of character?

91
00:06:22,821 --> 00:06:25,365
That pretty face has you
with your nose high in the air.

92
00:06:25,448 --> 00:06:28,159
You deserve to be struck down
by lightning from the heavens above.

93
00:06:28,243 --> 00:06:29,119
That's pretty harsh.

94
00:06:29,202 --> 00:06:31,997
You would curse someone
who was just senselessly attacked?

95
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,415
I know Mr. Cha

96
00:06:33,498 --> 00:06:35,959
can be a bit unreasonable at times,
but please bear with him.

97
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:38,962
Yes. He certainly is
an impulsive fool through and through.

98
00:06:39,462 --> 00:06:41,089
Working for him must be torture.

99
00:06:42,132 --> 00:06:44,300
Let's go, Ms. Shin. I'll take you home.

100
00:06:47,262 --> 00:06:48,638
In this moving palanquin?

101
00:06:48,722 --> 00:06:50,432
Hear me!

102
00:06:52,267 --> 00:06:53,268
Shall we?

103
00:06:58,690 --> 00:07:01,818
Mr. Cha, this is
the CCTV footage from the scene.

104
00:07:03,486 --> 00:07:04,696
Why would they do this?

105
00:07:06,281 --> 00:07:07,949
I thought it had already been handled.

106
00:07:08,033 --> 00:07:09,117
<i>Sir,</i>

107
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,744
about that protester from earlier--

108
00:07:10,827 --> 00:07:12,245
Can it wait?

109
00:07:12,328 --> 00:07:13,496
I need to make a call.

110
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:14,789
Yes, sir.

111
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:16,791
Mr. Son.

112
00:07:17,584 --> 00:07:19,461
Let's just handle the guy
from the lobby earlier.

113
00:07:19,544 --> 00:07:20,712
How exactly?

114
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,466
You said it was about unpaid wages.

115
00:07:24,549 --> 00:07:25,925
Just resolve it for them.

116
00:07:27,594 --> 00:07:29,345
Is there someone behind the scenes?

117
00:07:29,929 --> 00:07:31,264
Any guesses on the motive?

118
00:07:31,931 --> 00:07:33,391
I assume it's money.

119
00:07:33,475 --> 00:07:36,436
They attacked even after they were paid
what they were owed.

120
00:07:37,145 --> 00:07:38,855
There's a bigger payout somewhere.

121
00:07:46,696 --> 00:07:49,365
He just slammed the door in my face
as if I were some assassin.

122
00:07:49,449 --> 00:07:50,784
What is he scheming now?

123
00:07:50,867 --> 00:07:52,452
Is he having me watched? Is that it?

124
00:07:52,535 --> 00:07:54,079
No, not at all.

125
00:07:54,162 --> 00:07:55,330
Mr. Cha was worried about you.

126
00:07:55,413 --> 00:07:58,083
He asked me to make sure
you got home safely.

127
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:01,127
He was worried about me?

128
00:08:01,211 --> 00:08:03,421
When I reviewed your profile,
I noticed you lived nearby.

129
00:08:03,505 --> 00:08:06,007
I mean, you were almost
in a car accident earlier.

130
00:08:06,091 --> 00:08:07,092
And had the audition too.

131
00:08:07,175 --> 00:08:10,011
You've been through a lot today,
so he was concerned.

132
00:08:11,763 --> 00:08:13,139
In this desolate world,

133
00:08:13,807 --> 00:08:15,809
I guess I have someone
who worries about me.

134
00:08:15,892 --> 00:08:18,311
Too bad he is the cause of my distress.

135
00:08:21,231 --> 00:08:22,565
Ms. Shin, are you okay?

136
00:08:22,649 --> 00:08:24,400
You look a little pale.

137
00:08:24,484 --> 00:08:26,653
Well, actually,

138
00:08:26,736 --> 00:08:29,531
I have wanted to ask you this
for some time now.

139
00:08:29,614 --> 00:08:31,449
Could you slow down a bit?

140
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:33,701
This palanquin is moving way too fast.

141
00:08:33,785 --> 00:08:34,911
It is making me very dizzy.

142
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:41,668
But we're only going
20km an hour right now.

143
00:08:46,381 --> 00:08:47,423
In all my life,

144
00:08:47,507 --> 00:08:50,093
I have never been in a palanquin
that went this fast.

145
00:09:01,229 --> 00:09:02,397
Father.

146
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,690
Is this seafood stew?

147
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:05,400
Seafood herbal chicken stew.

148
00:09:05,483 --> 00:09:08,653
Made with 100% wild-caught abalone.

149
00:09:08,736 --> 00:09:11,156
I took the first flight to Jeju Island
at the crack of dawn

150
00:09:11,239 --> 00:09:12,866
just to get this for you.

151
00:09:12,949 --> 00:09:15,201
-I didn't sleep a wink.
-You can be so silly.

152
00:09:15,285 --> 00:09:16,494
Did you already forget

153
00:09:16,578 --> 00:09:19,205
that Father caught that awful norovirus
from eating raw oysters

154
00:09:19,289 --> 00:09:21,166
at his birthday last year?

155
00:09:21,249 --> 00:09:22,584
You know he has a weak stomach.

156
00:09:27,213 --> 00:09:29,007
What hearty roots.

157
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:30,967
Abalones are so basic.

158
00:09:31,593 --> 00:09:33,761
You should have one before the meal.

159
00:09:33,845 --> 00:09:36,097
It's genuine wild ginseng harvested
by a ginseng forager

160
00:09:36,181 --> 00:09:37,390
on Mount Jiri.

161
00:09:37,473 --> 00:09:39,184
It has a nice bitterness to it.

162
00:09:39,934 --> 00:09:41,436
That's the real deal.

163
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,063
I can't compete with you two.

164
00:09:44,147 --> 00:09:46,649
Next time you prepare a gift for Uncle,

165
00:09:46,733 --> 00:09:47,901
can you include me?

166
00:09:47,984 --> 00:09:49,319
Sure thing, Mun-do.

167
00:09:49,402 --> 00:09:51,029
It's a bit rude to show up empty-handed

168
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:52,572
to your uncle's birthday party, no?

169
00:09:52,655 --> 00:09:54,407
Don't talk to Mun-do about manners.

170
00:09:54,490 --> 00:09:57,243
Ten kids don't compare
to one good nephew.

171
00:09:57,327 --> 00:09:59,329
Here we go again.

172
00:09:59,412 --> 00:10:00,830
That damn liver story.

173
00:10:00,914 --> 00:10:04,250
17 YEARS AGO

174
00:10:04,334 --> 00:10:07,503
All right, who's going to give me a liver?

175
00:10:07,587 --> 00:10:09,923
If it weren't for this godforsaken asthma,

176
00:10:10,006 --> 00:10:13,593
I would gladly give you as many pieces
of my liver as you wanted.

177
00:10:15,637 --> 00:10:17,847
If I just weren't breastfeeding the kids,

178
00:10:18,389 --> 00:10:21,100
I would gladly chop mine off for you.

179
00:10:21,768 --> 00:10:23,561
I'll give you mine, Uncle.

180
00:10:31,694 --> 00:10:35,031
While my perfectly healthy kids
turned their backs on me,

181
00:10:35,114 --> 00:10:37,158
my nephew gave me a second chance at life.

182
00:10:37,242 --> 00:10:40,328
And you brats can't even show
gratitude to your father's savior.

183
00:10:40,411 --> 00:10:41,621
Uncle, please stop.

184
00:10:41,704 --> 00:10:43,957
Se-gye was too young back then,

185
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:46,584
and the rest all had valid reasons.

186
00:10:46,668 --> 00:10:48,670
All I had to offer was my health anyway.

187
00:10:48,753 --> 00:10:51,130
Yes, I'm only alive
because of you, Mun-do.

188
00:10:51,214 --> 00:10:52,674
What a shame.

189
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:56,135
How nice it would be if Se-gye
were even half the man you are.

190
00:11:12,193 --> 00:11:14,696
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

191
00:11:15,363 --> 00:11:18,074
<i>It appears I still had</i>
<i>surprises waiting for me.</i>

192
00:11:18,658 --> 00:11:21,703
Mr. Cha insisted
that you get checked out by a doctor.

193
00:11:21,786 --> 00:11:23,705
The aftereffects of a car accident
really get you.

194
00:11:23,788 --> 00:11:25,123
Make sure you go tomorrow.

195
00:11:32,255 --> 00:11:34,632
After rebuffing me so harshly to my face…

196
00:11:35,675 --> 00:11:38,303
He certainly is a man
riddled with contradictions.

197
00:11:47,186 --> 00:11:50,148
What a destitute life this woman leads.

198
00:11:50,815 --> 00:11:52,233
You call this a house?

199
00:11:55,570 --> 00:11:56,904
I have arrived!

200
00:11:57,488 --> 00:11:59,032
Look at that freak. She must be wasted.

201
00:11:59,115 --> 00:12:01,242
Like she's a noblewoman or something?

202
00:12:01,326 --> 00:12:02,410
-I know, right?
-Hey…

203
00:12:02,994 --> 00:12:04,495
I have arrived!

204
00:12:04,579 --> 00:12:05,580
Is anybody in there?

205
00:12:06,456 --> 00:12:08,875
My word. Is this any way to treat
the master of the house?

206
00:12:08,958 --> 00:12:10,668
What is the gatekeeper even doing?

207
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:15,506
That light turned on by itself.

208
00:12:22,555 --> 00:12:23,514
Hold on…

209
00:12:25,016 --> 00:12:26,559
I need to gather my wits about me.

210
00:12:26,642 --> 00:12:29,687
Keep your wits about you,
and you can survive even a tiger's den.

211
00:12:29,771 --> 00:12:32,023
"With a focused mind,
nothing is impossible."

212
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:35,485
Unit 203!

213
00:12:36,152 --> 00:12:38,905
Where have you been?
Why are you getting back so late?

214
00:12:38,988 --> 00:12:40,490
And why is your phone off?

215
00:12:40,573 --> 00:12:43,618
Hurry upstairs. Your grandmother
has been waiting for ages.

216
00:12:43,701 --> 00:12:45,161
Just to see your face.

217
00:12:45,244 --> 00:12:46,245
Grandmother?

218
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,170
My goodness.

219
00:12:56,589 --> 00:12:58,049
There's my little girl.

220
00:12:59,258 --> 00:13:00,718
Come and sit down.

221
00:13:02,470 --> 00:13:03,721
Sit. Go on.

222
00:13:04,222 --> 00:13:06,891
You didn't even have time to change?
What is all this?

223
00:13:12,772 --> 00:13:13,773
All right.

224
00:13:13,856 --> 00:13:15,566
Here. Try this.

225
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:18,152
I made your favorites.
<i>Japchae </i>and pork cutlets.

226
00:13:18,236 --> 00:13:20,154
I even made candied sweet potatoes.

227
00:13:23,616 --> 00:13:25,660
<i>Come to think of it,</i>
<i>I have not eaten all day.</i>

228
00:13:25,743 --> 00:13:26,828
I fried them myself.

229
00:13:32,834 --> 00:13:34,252
<i>They say a person's hands</i>

230
00:13:34,877 --> 00:13:36,754
<i>reveal the life they have lived.</i>

231
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:39,132
Why do you look so worn out?

232
00:13:39,632 --> 00:13:41,467
<i>It seems this woman's grandmother</i>

233
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:43,428
<i>did not have an easy life either.</i>

234
00:13:43,511 --> 00:13:45,513
Did work keep you from eating again?

235
00:13:46,139 --> 00:13:47,515
Hurry up and eat.

236
00:13:48,141 --> 00:13:50,017
Here, take these and eat.

237
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:53,479
Oh right.
You should join us for a bite too.

238
00:13:53,563 --> 00:13:56,524
-Really? Yes. Thank you so much.
-Sure.

239
00:13:57,692 --> 00:13:58,734
Thank you.

240
00:14:11,664 --> 00:14:13,791
Silly me. How could I be so forgetful?

241
00:14:13,875 --> 00:14:16,669
I'm on this herbal supplement, you see.

242
00:14:16,752 --> 00:14:19,213
So I don't think
I should be eating all this meat.

243
00:14:19,297 --> 00:14:20,506
But there's no meat in this.

244
00:14:20,590 --> 00:14:22,049
No, I'm fine. Really.

245
00:14:22,592 --> 00:14:24,510
Enjoy your meal, Unit 203.

246
00:14:25,094 --> 00:14:26,679
-Excuse me.
-Sure.

247
00:14:29,765 --> 00:14:30,808
Goodness.

248
00:14:34,979 --> 00:14:35,938
Here.

249
00:14:36,481 --> 00:14:39,066
Don't share this with anyone.

250
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:42,487
Hide it in a corner somewhere
and eat it all by yourself. Got it?

251
00:14:42,570 --> 00:14:45,239
This isn't pork. It's beef.
High-quality Korean beef.

252
00:14:45,323 --> 00:14:46,449
See. Korean beef.

253
00:15:01,047 --> 00:15:02,882
Is it good? Do you like it?

254
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:05,968
You know, I've been messing up
the seasoning lately.

255
00:15:06,052 --> 00:15:07,762
I put extra effort into this one.

256
00:15:09,096 --> 00:15:10,223
It is quite delicious.

257
00:15:10,306 --> 00:15:11,682
Really?

258
00:15:11,766 --> 00:15:13,017
Gosh.

259
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:14,519
Great. Go on.

260
00:15:14,602 --> 00:15:15,645
Eat up.

261
00:15:15,728 --> 00:15:18,147
Go on now. Have some <i>japchae</i> too.

262
00:15:22,735 --> 00:15:24,362
Have some more.

263
00:15:26,405 --> 00:15:27,907
You must have been starving.

264
00:15:34,372 --> 00:15:37,208
How nice it is to have
everyone gather for a meal like this.

265
00:15:37,291 --> 00:15:39,835
Asking the family to gather
for a measly meal on my birthday

266
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:41,587
is not asking for the moon.

267
00:15:41,671 --> 00:15:45,424
And yet, I don't even know
if the one grandson I have will show up.

268
00:15:46,092 --> 00:15:47,468
Father, you saw the news, right?

269
00:15:47,552 --> 00:15:49,929
I mean, he is way too old
to be acting out like that.

270
00:15:50,012 --> 00:15:52,056
I guess he still can't control
that temper of his.

271
00:15:52,139 --> 00:15:53,432
They say the video was doctored.

272
00:15:53,516 --> 00:15:55,226
Looks like someone was messing with him.

273
00:15:55,309 --> 00:15:57,687
He's probably late
cleaning up that mess, Uncle.

274
00:15:58,312 --> 00:16:00,690
You sure know everything, don't you?

275
00:16:00,773 --> 00:16:03,818
Fake or not, he should've
just behaved himself all along.

276
00:16:03,901 --> 00:16:05,319
With that kind of reputation,

277
00:16:05,403 --> 00:16:08,447
people will believe anything,
no matter how outlandish or tawdry.

278
00:16:08,531 --> 00:16:09,865
Don't you agree, Father?

279
00:16:09,949 --> 00:16:11,450
Why that little…

280
00:16:22,712 --> 00:16:24,463
Happy birthday, Grandfather.

281
00:16:24,547 --> 00:16:26,048
Sorry I'm late. Car trouble.

282
00:16:26,132 --> 00:16:28,217
You should've planned ahead for that.

283
00:16:28,301 --> 00:16:30,386
A businessman should be able
to manage his time.

284
00:16:30,469 --> 00:16:33,180
I knew the party would start
with the usual catfight

285
00:16:33,264 --> 00:16:36,684
and shameless displays of loyalty.
Neither of which I can stomach.

286
00:16:36,767 --> 00:16:38,936
So I timed my arrival to avoid it.

287
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:39,979
Is it still going?

288
00:16:40,062 --> 00:16:41,272
You rotten scoundrel.

289
00:16:41,355 --> 00:16:42,440
Even at a birthday party,

290
00:16:42,523 --> 00:16:45,026
you can't keep that trap of yours shut?

291
00:16:45,109 --> 00:16:48,112
Please try to calm down, Uncle.
It's your birthday, after all.

292
00:16:50,197 --> 00:16:51,198
Welcome, Se-gye.

293
00:16:56,287 --> 00:16:57,246
Cheers.

294
00:16:58,831 --> 00:17:00,249
Sir, the CCTV footage

295
00:17:00,333 --> 00:17:04,337
from the rear entrance confirms
the attacker fled in a nearby getaway car.

296
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,048
It was parked too far away
for the cameras to catch the plate.

297
00:17:07,131 --> 00:17:08,299
Just as I expected.

298
00:17:09,717 --> 00:17:11,469
Which means it wasn't a random attack.

299
00:17:11,552 --> 00:17:14,347
Sir, we should request
a police investigation now.

300
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:17,725
They timed their attack to coincide
with the buyer meeting and audition.

301
00:17:17,808 --> 00:17:20,853
It appears they were targeting
the "abusive CEO" image.

302
00:17:20,936 --> 00:17:21,896
That's why.

303
00:17:22,396 --> 00:17:24,565
The intent was underhanded
and premeditated.

304
00:17:25,524 --> 00:17:27,068
We can't just play into their hands.

305
00:17:27,151 --> 00:17:29,236
Is there someone you suspect?

306
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,780
There's no shortage of people

307
00:17:31,405 --> 00:17:33,366
who want to see me crash and burn.

308
00:17:34,909 --> 00:17:36,077
I suppose you're right.

309
00:17:39,288 --> 00:17:41,832
They all treat me like a thief
raiding the family vault.

310
00:17:41,916 --> 00:17:43,668
The eldest aunt, the youngest aunt,

311
00:17:43,751 --> 00:17:45,586
and even the distant cousin.

312
00:17:47,672 --> 00:17:50,257
This place is crawling with fake smiles.

313
00:17:54,887 --> 00:17:56,055
Seo-ri.

314
00:17:56,138 --> 00:17:59,183
You're all alone in this strange place.

315
00:17:59,266 --> 00:18:00,685
It must be hard.

316
00:18:01,644 --> 00:18:03,187
I know how you feel.

317
00:18:05,147 --> 00:18:07,149
My restaurant is doing well.

318
00:18:07,233 --> 00:18:10,277
Stop worrying about me
and buy yourself some new clothes.

319
00:18:10,361 --> 00:18:12,530
No young lady should be dressed like this.

320
00:18:12,613 --> 00:18:15,408
You'll never land a fellow
looking like that.

321
00:18:15,491 --> 00:18:17,702
As if having one ever leads
to anything good.

322
00:18:21,205 --> 00:18:24,083
You grew up so lonely
without your parents' love.

323
00:18:25,042 --> 00:18:27,670
You should have at least one person
on your side in this world.

324
00:18:27,753 --> 00:18:30,965
But still, you grew up to be
such a fine young lady.

325
00:18:31,048 --> 00:18:32,508
You've done such a great job.

326
00:18:35,302 --> 00:18:36,804
I'm so proud of you.

327
00:18:39,181 --> 00:18:41,851
Are you proud of your granddaughter?

328
00:18:42,351 --> 00:18:43,352
Of course.

329
00:18:44,687 --> 00:18:47,690
You're so beautiful inside and out.

330
00:18:47,773 --> 00:18:49,775
In all my time on this earth,

331
00:18:49,859 --> 00:18:51,986
I've never met anyone like you.

332
00:18:55,448 --> 00:18:56,741
Hurry inside.

333
00:18:56,824 --> 00:18:57,908
I'll be going now.

334
00:18:58,993 --> 00:18:59,994
Go on.

335
00:19:12,923 --> 00:19:14,300
Go inside.

336
00:19:18,345 --> 00:19:19,472
Safe…

337
00:19:21,474 --> 00:19:22,892
travels.

338
00:19:36,947 --> 00:19:38,532
-Mr. Son.
-Yes, sir.

339
00:19:39,033 --> 00:19:41,410
Twice can't be a coincidence, right?

340
00:19:43,078 --> 00:19:44,121
Pardon?

341
00:19:44,955 --> 00:19:46,040
Think about it.

342
00:19:46,707 --> 00:19:49,210
She passed out in front of my car
when it was barely moving,

343
00:19:49,293 --> 00:19:51,712
and then she predicted
that attack like some sort of psychic.

344
00:19:51,796 --> 00:19:53,923
I looked into Ms. Shin Seo-ri.

345
00:19:54,423 --> 00:19:57,426
Besides her rude speech,
nothing else seemed suspicious.

346
00:19:57,510 --> 00:20:00,554
Surely you don't think
someone put her up to this?

347
00:20:00,638 --> 00:20:02,223
It never hurts to be careful.

348
00:20:03,015 --> 00:20:05,184
We've put everything on the line
for this brand launch,

349
00:20:05,267 --> 00:20:07,311
even shouldering private fund risk.

350
00:20:07,394 --> 00:20:09,730
We need to be
extra cautious right now.

351
00:20:11,232 --> 00:20:13,192
Double the security team for now,

352
00:20:13,818 --> 00:20:16,153
and personally double-check
all the HR files.

353
00:20:16,237 --> 00:20:17,238
Yes, sir.

354
00:20:18,948 --> 00:20:21,450
And find out
everything you can about her.

355
00:20:21,534 --> 00:20:22,576
Yes, sir.

356
00:20:43,973 --> 00:20:45,266
You call this a room?

357
00:20:46,475 --> 00:20:48,644
A prison cell would be more luxurious.

358
00:20:53,691 --> 00:20:54,733
What in the world…

359
00:20:55,234 --> 00:20:56,110
<i>Look here.</i>

360
00:20:56,193 --> 00:20:59,071
No window ought to command such a view.

361
00:20:59,154 --> 00:21:02,616
Seriously? Were you expecting
a view of Namsan Tower or something?

362
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:04,702
Why are you complaining now?

363
00:21:04,785 --> 00:21:07,329
It's compact and great value.

364
00:21:07,413 --> 00:21:08,581
With ventilation, no less!

365
00:21:08,664 --> 00:21:10,749
I gave you our most popular room.

366
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,877
You call <i>this</i> a room and collect rent?

367
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,212
I have never encountered
such miserliness in my life.

368
00:21:15,296 --> 00:21:18,549
All the windowless rooms are taken now.

369
00:21:18,632 --> 00:21:20,467
You can move when one opens up.

370
00:21:21,176 --> 00:21:22,344
Wait.

371
00:21:22,428 --> 00:21:24,555
There are even rooms without windows?

372
00:21:24,638 --> 00:21:25,806
Unbelievable.

373
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:27,558
I never!

374
00:21:29,143 --> 00:21:30,352
My goodness.

375
00:21:41,322 --> 00:21:42,489
Why, this scoundrel…

376
00:21:56,337 --> 00:21:57,755
Unit 203, open up!

377
00:21:57,838 --> 00:21:59,340
Open this door!

378
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:01,133
Unbelievable.

379
00:22:01,216 --> 00:22:02,384
Who goes there?

380
00:22:02,468 --> 00:22:04,887
What sort of knave batters
a lady's door in the dead of night?

381
00:22:04,970 --> 00:22:06,597
"Knave"? Seriously?

382
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:08,724
You know, I've tolerated
all your noise until now,

383
00:22:08,807 --> 00:22:10,142
but I can't take it anymore!

384
00:22:10,225 --> 00:22:13,187
You keep rustling around,
and you won't stop talking to yourself.

385
00:22:13,270 --> 00:22:14,396
I can't live like this.

386
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:17,066
If you cannot live with that,
you should just leave.

387
00:22:17,650 --> 00:22:19,193
Have you lost your damn mind?

388
00:22:19,276 --> 00:22:21,570
Are you trying to start a fight with me?

389
00:22:21,654 --> 00:22:24,657
You can hear every burp
and fart from your neighbors here.

390
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:27,618
Wouldn't it be common courtesy
to be a bit more careful?

391
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:29,578
What the… Hold on.

392
00:22:29,662 --> 00:22:30,829
What's going on here?

393
00:22:30,913 --> 00:22:32,414
What's with all this racket?

394
00:22:32,498 --> 00:22:35,459
This man here is making
the most absurd complaints.

395
00:22:35,542 --> 00:22:37,962
He says not to burp
or fart too loudly in my own room.

396
00:22:38,045 --> 00:22:41,256
Why not just tell me
to stop breathing altogether?

397
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:42,633
Unbelievable.

398
00:22:42,716 --> 00:22:44,635
You clearly missed the point.

399
00:22:44,718 --> 00:22:46,887
We are trapped in this prison together.

400
00:22:46,971 --> 00:22:48,973
If we cannot show a little grace

401
00:22:49,056 --> 00:22:51,016
and forgive small faults,

402
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:53,352
how are we any different from beasts?

403
00:22:53,435 --> 00:22:54,395
"Beasts"?

404
00:22:54,478 --> 00:22:56,647
So are you saying
I'm some kind of savage now?

405
00:22:56,730 --> 00:22:58,190
Mencius said

406
00:22:58,273 --> 00:23:01,151
that a sense of shame and indignation
is the beginning of righteousness.

407
00:23:01,235 --> 00:23:04,363
You fail to see your own flaws
and only harp on others.

408
00:23:05,197 --> 00:23:08,242
Like a crap-covered dog
scolding a dusty dog.

409
00:23:08,325 --> 00:23:09,994
Crap dog? You calling me a mutt?

410
00:23:10,077 --> 00:23:12,121
-Hear, hear!
-Hear, hear!

411
00:23:12,204 --> 00:23:13,455
Who was that?

412
00:23:15,124 --> 00:23:17,835
I ought to wring your neck,
but it seems

413
00:23:17,918 --> 00:23:19,545
I have public sentiment on my side.

414
00:23:19,628 --> 00:23:21,630
So stop causing a scene and begone!

415
00:23:22,548 --> 00:23:24,591
My day has been long enough.

416
00:23:30,389 --> 00:23:32,725
She couldn't even look me
in the eye before.

417
00:23:32,808 --> 00:23:34,435
What's gotten into her?

418
00:23:50,284 --> 00:23:51,910
<i>I just sensed an assassin's presence.</i>

419
00:23:51,994 --> 00:23:54,288
<i>Someone nearby is after your life!</i>
<i>Get down!</i>

420
00:24:00,461 --> 00:24:01,879
<i>Keep me by your side.</i>

421
00:24:02,463 --> 00:24:05,591
<i>I shall safeguard</i>
<i>the flickering flame you call your life.</i>

422
00:24:05,674 --> 00:24:07,593
As if she could keep anyone safe.

423
00:24:18,645 --> 00:24:20,522
How truly marvelous.

424
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:23,567
This is pure witchcraft.

425
00:24:26,862 --> 00:24:28,781
If you pull the string,

426
00:24:28,864 --> 00:24:30,866
it lights right up.

427
00:24:32,159 --> 00:24:33,827
How useful.

428
00:24:37,247 --> 00:24:39,166
<i>You tell me to leave because I am useless?</i>

429
00:24:39,249 --> 00:24:41,335
<i>Do you think Court Lady Kim</i>
<i>took a bribe?</i>

430
00:24:41,418 --> 00:24:44,338
<i>I cannot understand</i>
<i>why she brought in someone like you.</i>

431
00:24:44,421 --> 00:24:46,256
Who are you to decide my worth?

432
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:48,467
Look at the venom in her eyes.

433
00:24:48,550 --> 00:24:50,677
Jumping into that river
must have been easy for you.

434
00:24:50,761 --> 00:24:53,097
I heard you ran away
after being sold into slavery.

435
00:24:53,180 --> 00:24:55,516
A lowly wench like you
should know her place.

436
00:24:55,599 --> 00:24:57,684
How could we ever share a room
with someone like you?

437
00:24:57,768 --> 00:24:59,228
-So vile.
-What did you say?

438
00:24:59,311 --> 00:25:00,437
Did you just call me vile?

439
00:25:00,521 --> 00:25:03,315
Looks like you grew up sheltered
and do not know any better.

440
00:25:03,398 --> 00:25:06,110
Allow me to show you
what something truly "vile" looks like.

441
00:25:08,612 --> 00:25:09,530
My goodness!

442
00:25:14,827 --> 00:25:17,079
Just try calling me vile again.

443
00:25:17,621 --> 00:25:19,331
I will pour it over your heads next time!

444
00:25:19,414 --> 00:25:20,874
Have you lost your damn mind?

445
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:24,962
Grab her!

446
00:25:25,838 --> 00:25:27,840
Let go of me! You cannot be serious!

447
00:25:27,923 --> 00:25:29,883
The palace follows a set of laws.

448
00:25:29,967 --> 00:25:32,511
Even the Inner Court's lowest ranks
have a hierarchy.

449
00:25:32,594 --> 00:25:35,222
Let me give you a proper lesson
on those laws today.

450
00:25:35,305 --> 00:25:37,057
You two, drag her out.

451
00:25:38,225 --> 00:25:39,184
Let me go!

452
00:25:39,893 --> 00:25:41,019
Let me go!

453
00:25:51,655 --> 00:25:53,073
Let me out this instant!

454
00:25:53,157 --> 00:25:54,283
Let me out!

455
00:25:54,366 --> 00:25:55,742
Grab that rock.

456
00:25:58,704 --> 00:25:59,997
Let me out!

457
00:26:00,622 --> 00:26:01,665
Let me out!

458
00:26:13,343 --> 00:26:14,845
Why is she so quiet?

459
00:26:14,928 --> 00:26:18,265
I heard she was a little crazy.
What if something is wrong with her?

460
00:26:19,391 --> 00:26:21,685
Who cares? She deserves it.

461
00:26:21,768 --> 00:26:24,146
She should have just left
when we asked nicely.

462
00:26:25,898 --> 00:26:26,857
Let us go.

463
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:49,379
Now I will not have to stay up
every night…

464
00:26:51,465 --> 00:26:53,258
tending the lamp.

465
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:58,805
That scoundrel still has not come
to his senses.

466
00:26:58,889 --> 00:27:01,600
I should have snapped his wrists
when I had the chance.

467
00:27:04,603 --> 00:27:05,812
How will I ever

468
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:08,982
get any sleep with all this commotion?

469
00:27:28,961 --> 00:27:33,131
YEONGHWI CHAMBER

470
00:27:50,649 --> 00:27:52,526
Please let me out!

471
00:28:24,933 --> 00:28:26,685
<i>Just look at this household.</i>

472
00:28:27,602 --> 00:28:31,356
<i>Not so much as a piece of gold</i>
<i>or a simple jade ring to be found.</i>

473
00:29:02,471 --> 00:29:03,680
<i>I am an actor.</i>

474
00:29:04,514 --> 00:29:06,141
<i>A former child star</i>

475
00:29:06,892 --> 00:29:08,894
<i>who no one recognizes anymore.</i>

476
00:29:10,562 --> 00:29:14,941
<i>I'm just a nobody with no ties</i>
<i>to the mythical rise of K-dramas.</i>

477
00:29:15,025 --> 00:29:16,693
Harder. One more.

478
00:29:16,777 --> 00:29:18,904
-Cut! Turn it around!
-Let's turn it around.

479
00:29:18,987 --> 00:29:21,615
Who is she?
Where did they even find her?

480
00:29:21,698 --> 00:29:23,492
-Let's clean this up.
-Okay.

481
00:29:24,868 --> 00:29:25,827
Hurry up.

482
00:29:25,911 --> 00:29:27,245
WE'RE ROOTING FOR YOUR DREAMS

483
00:29:27,371 --> 00:29:30,582
<i>The world likes to admire dreamers…</i>

484
00:29:30,665 --> 00:29:31,917
BALANCE: 164,019 WON

485
00:29:33,001 --> 00:29:36,088
<i>…but even encouragement has its limits.</i>

486
00:29:37,798 --> 00:29:41,343
FUNDS TO WIRE TO NAM OK-SUN
50,000 WON

487
00:29:44,012 --> 00:29:45,806
FUNDS TO WIRE TO NAM OK-SUN
100,000 WON

488
00:29:45,889 --> 00:29:46,765
TRANSACTION COMPLETED

489
00:29:50,227 --> 00:29:51,103
GRANDMA

490
00:29:53,688 --> 00:29:55,899
-Grandma.
<i>-Hey, Seo-ri.</i>

491
00:29:55,982 --> 00:29:57,651
I just sent you some money.

492
00:29:58,527 --> 00:30:01,530
So treat yourself to a nice meal.
Don't go asking around for scraps.

493
00:30:01,613 --> 00:30:04,908
<i>Gosh, I'm just an old lady.</i>
<i>I wouldn't even know where to spend it.</i>

494
00:30:04,991 --> 00:30:06,576
Hey, keep it down!

495
00:30:06,660 --> 00:30:07,953
<i>What was that noise?</i>

496
00:30:08,036 --> 00:30:09,413
<i>Are you with someone?</i>

497
00:30:09,496 --> 00:30:11,206
No. That's just the TV.

498
00:30:12,916 --> 00:30:15,460
You've got great hearing.
How did you even hear that?

499
00:30:15,544 --> 00:30:17,462
<i>My eyes and ears still work just fine.</i>

500
00:30:17,546 --> 00:30:20,340
<i>I have to stay healthy</i>
<i>if I want to see you on TV.</i>

501
00:30:20,424 --> 00:30:23,468
Grandma, I'm going to make it big on TV.

502
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,305
You just wait and see.

503
00:30:27,848 --> 00:30:30,267
<i>Of course. I'm so proud of you.</i>

504
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:38,316
<i>My grandma always tells me</i>
<i>she's proud of me.</i>

505
00:30:39,943 --> 00:30:41,486
<i>But whenever I hear that,</i>

506
00:30:42,112 --> 00:30:44,656
<i>it makes me feel small</i>
<i>for some odd reason.</i>

507
00:30:46,616 --> 00:30:49,369
<i>I'm just a burden of a granddaughter</i>
<i>who can't let go</i>

508
00:30:49,453 --> 00:30:51,496
<i>of a dream that will never come true.</i>

509
00:30:51,580 --> 00:30:53,665
<i>What is there to be proud of?</i>

510
00:30:53,748 --> 00:30:57,419
<i>How has she made it this far</i>
<i>without earning any real money?</i>

511
00:30:58,879 --> 00:31:01,131
What a pitiful diary.

512
00:31:01,214 --> 00:31:04,885
She wrote down every trivial detail,
as if it were something to be proud of.

513
00:31:06,178 --> 00:31:09,890
No wonder every bastard she meets
tries to walk all over her.

514
00:31:14,936 --> 00:31:17,981
SLEEP IS FOR THE DEAD

515
00:31:18,064 --> 00:31:19,065
THE FUTURE LEADING LADY

516
00:31:19,149 --> 00:31:20,192
YOU WILL BECOME A STAR

517
00:31:20,275 --> 00:31:22,277
I WILL GIVE MY GRANDMA A GOOD LIFE

518
00:31:24,070 --> 00:31:25,614
I'm so proud of you.

519
00:31:52,307 --> 00:31:54,684
<i>A peony, beaded with dewdrops</i>
<i>like pearls, was plucked</i>

520
00:31:54,768 --> 00:31:56,728
<i>by a beauty as she passed a window.</i>

521
00:31:57,687 --> 00:31:59,105
<i>No flower in the world</i>

522
00:31:59,189 --> 00:32:01,650
<i>could be as beautiful as you.</i>

523
00:32:03,401 --> 00:32:05,987
<i>"Royal Consort Hui of the Kang clan,</i>
<i>of the Inner Court,</i>

524
00:32:06,071 --> 00:32:08,323
<i>has committed a heinous crime."</i>

525
00:32:08,823 --> 00:32:11,868
<i>Royal Consort Hui shall come forth</i>
<i>and receive the royal command!</i>

526
00:32:15,789 --> 00:32:17,207
<i>They say</i>

527
00:32:18,833 --> 00:32:20,919
<i>no blossom endures its bloom forever.</i>

528
00:32:27,968 --> 00:32:29,135
<i>The Three Obediences.</i>

529
00:32:30,345 --> 00:32:31,721
<i>Obey your father.</i>

530
00:32:32,347 --> 00:32:33,932
<i>Obey your husband.</i>

531
00:32:34,724 --> 00:32:37,394
<i>And obey your son.</i>
<i>That is what is expected of women.</i>

532
00:32:37,477 --> 00:32:38,979
<i>Rather than clinging pitifully</i>

533
00:32:39,563 --> 00:32:42,357
<i>to a wretched life with no one to rely on,</i>

534
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:45,068
<i>perhaps death would be…</i>

535
00:32:45,652 --> 00:32:46,903
Better, my foot!

536
00:32:46,987 --> 00:32:49,114
Even if I am wallowing in dog crap,

537
00:32:49,197 --> 00:32:50,782
life is better than death.

538
00:32:51,658 --> 00:32:52,951
So in this life,

539
00:32:53,034 --> 00:32:55,203
I will do what I must to survive it.

540
00:32:56,204 --> 00:32:58,373
That will also be how I honor the one

541
00:32:59,249 --> 00:33:00,875
to whom this body truly belongs.

542
00:33:36,536 --> 00:33:39,039
<i>I will tell you all about it,</i>
<i>so try not to doze off</i>

543
00:33:39,122 --> 00:33:41,082
<i>and listen well.</i>

544
00:33:43,251 --> 00:33:45,086
<i>Whenever foreign enemies invaded,</i>

545
00:33:45,170 --> 00:33:48,131
<i>the people always stepped up</i>
<i>to fight before anyone else.</i>

546
00:33:48,798 --> 00:33:50,592
<i>-If they had no guns, they used swords.</i>
-Gosh.

547
00:33:50,675 --> 00:33:53,345
<i>If they had no swords, they used rocks.</i>

548
00:33:55,263 --> 00:33:57,140
The country did nothing for them,

549
00:33:57,682 --> 00:34:00,018
yet they still sacrificed
their precious lives.

550
00:34:00,644 --> 00:34:01,519
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

551
00:34:01,603 --> 00:34:04,522
<i>due to treaties signed by a few traitors,</i>

552
00:34:04,606 --> 00:34:06,816
<i>the country lost its sovereignty!</i>

553
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:09,402
Those traitors deserve
to be torn limb from limb!

554
00:34:09,486 --> 00:34:11,613
They should be torn to pieces!

555
00:34:15,867 --> 00:34:17,952
<i>Long live Korean Independence!</i>

556
00:34:18,036 --> 00:34:20,455
<i>Long live Korean Independence!</i>

557
00:34:20,538 --> 00:34:23,041
<i>-Long live Korean Independence!</i>
<i>-Long live Korean Independence!</i>

558
00:34:23,124 --> 00:34:25,377
Long live Korean Independence.

559
00:34:27,170 --> 00:34:29,506
Long live Korean Independence!

560
00:34:29,589 --> 00:34:30,799
Long live!

561
00:34:30,882 --> 00:34:32,092
Long live Korean Independence!

562
00:34:32,175 --> 00:34:34,678
Long live Korean Independence!

563
00:34:34,761 --> 00:34:36,262
Long live!

564
00:34:37,722 --> 00:34:39,516
Republic of Korea!

565
00:34:41,142 --> 00:34:43,144
Hey! Hey, everyone!

566
00:34:43,228 --> 00:34:44,354
Everyone, come out!

567
00:34:44,437 --> 00:34:46,189
Come on, everybody!

568
00:34:46,898 --> 00:34:49,359
Did you see the miracle
of the Red Devils?

569
00:34:49,442 --> 00:34:51,611
We made the semifinals! The semifinals!

570
00:34:51,695 --> 00:34:53,530
Republic of Korea!

571
00:34:55,907 --> 00:34:57,784
What's her deal?
The semifinals were ages ago.

572
00:34:57,867 --> 00:35:00,829
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

573
00:35:00,912 --> 00:35:02,580
Curse this wretched fate of mine.

574
00:35:03,373 --> 00:35:06,209
I am stuck here washing clothes
like some lowly servant.

575
00:35:06,292 --> 00:35:07,836
Curse this fate.

576
00:35:29,023 --> 00:35:30,400
What the… blood!

577
00:35:32,902 --> 00:35:35,488
There are rats everywhere I go.

578
00:35:36,364 --> 00:35:37,240
Did you see that?

579
00:35:37,866 --> 00:35:39,826
She just threw that bat at his head.

580
00:35:39,909 --> 00:35:41,619
That was amazing.

581
00:35:56,843 --> 00:35:57,969
SHIN SEO-RI

582
00:35:59,471 --> 00:36:01,514
<i>To the one coveting my side dishes,</i>

583
00:36:01,598 --> 00:36:03,308
<i>I cast a death curse last night.</i>

584
00:36:03,391 --> 00:36:06,978
<i>If you wish to avoid an untimely death,</i>
<i>return it to its rightful place.</i>

585
00:36:07,061 --> 00:36:08,229
Death curse, my foot.

586
00:36:08,772 --> 00:36:10,482
Pork collar and jowl, here I come.

587
00:36:11,733 --> 00:36:13,067
Got you now.

588
00:36:13,151 --> 00:36:14,277
I knew it was you.

589
00:36:15,612 --> 00:36:17,280
The containers look similar.

590
00:36:17,363 --> 00:36:18,865
I just got confused for a second.

591
00:36:18,948 --> 00:36:20,950
See. They all look alike.

592
00:36:21,576 --> 00:36:23,620
Are your eyes attached to your feet?

593
00:36:23,703 --> 00:36:25,830
Or are you just completely illiterate?

594
00:36:26,539 --> 00:36:29,501
My name is clearly written on it.
How dare you feign ignorance?

595
00:36:29,584 --> 00:36:32,045
-What's going on?
-He got caught stealing side dishes.

596
00:36:32,128 --> 00:36:35,256
Did he steal
my leftover <i>jokbal</i> and whelk too?

597
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:37,383
What's wrong with you all?
Do you have any proof?

598
00:36:37,467 --> 00:36:38,593
Do you?

599
00:36:38,676 --> 00:36:39,844
Don't point fingers.

600
00:36:39,928 --> 00:36:41,596
I can't believe this.

601
00:36:43,306 --> 00:36:44,933
Now that I have caught the rat,

602
00:36:45,016 --> 00:36:47,393
you may all rest easy
and partake of your meal.

603
00:36:47,477 --> 00:36:48,812
Amazing.

604
00:36:48,895 --> 00:36:51,856
Unit 203 just caught
the rooftop pervert too!

605
00:36:51,940 --> 00:36:55,401
She threw that laundry bat
like a shot put.

606
00:36:55,485 --> 00:36:57,153
I saw the whole thing.

607
00:37:01,282 --> 00:37:03,618
No need.
I did nothing to merit such fuss.

608
00:37:10,333 --> 00:37:12,293
BEST WISHES ON YOUR OPENING
CHOI MUN-DO, CHAIL E&amp;C

609
00:37:14,003 --> 00:37:15,171
Hey.

610
00:37:15,922 --> 00:37:16,798
Jeong-hyeon.

611
00:37:17,799 --> 00:37:18,967
Congratulations.

612
00:37:19,717 --> 00:37:21,970
I should've come by sooner.
That was thoughtless of me.

613
00:37:22,053 --> 00:37:25,223
Thoughtless? You sent a plant
and even some cash.

614
00:37:25,306 --> 00:37:27,725
I shamelessly
and happily accepted them.

615
00:37:27,809 --> 00:37:30,103
I thought you were only good
at caring for people,

616
00:37:30,186 --> 00:37:32,063
but you're good with plants too.

617
00:37:32,146 --> 00:37:33,940
Then again,
you've always been very attentive.

618
00:37:34,023 --> 00:37:36,734
You even put up
with someone as finicky as Se-gye.

619
00:37:38,695 --> 00:37:40,572
How is Se-gye doing these days?

620
00:37:55,211 --> 00:37:57,255
A plant? That's so not him.

621
00:37:57,338 --> 00:37:58,631
-Cash would've been better.
-Yeah.

622
00:37:58,715 --> 00:38:00,758
He gave me some cash, too. Mun-do.

623
00:38:01,301 --> 00:38:03,136
A cash gift for the clinic opening.

624
00:38:03,219 --> 00:38:04,304
Nothing in life is free.

625
00:38:04,387 --> 00:38:06,556
Free money always comes
with a high interest rate.

626
00:38:06,639 --> 00:38:08,892
Don't worry.
As if Mun-do would ever do that.

627
00:38:09,517 --> 00:38:11,394
Enough about me.
Let's go back to your story.

628
00:38:11,477 --> 00:38:13,354
-What story?
-About that weird woman.

629
00:38:13,438 --> 00:38:16,482
That woman in a shaman's <i>hanbok</i>
jumped in front of your car,

630
00:38:16,566 --> 00:38:18,776
showed up at your company,
predicted that attack,

631
00:38:18,860 --> 00:38:20,486
and she even offered to protect you?

632
00:38:20,570 --> 00:38:22,280
What do you think her deal is?

633
00:38:23,031 --> 00:38:26,492
She's really getting on my nerves.
Like a splinter under my fingernail.

634
00:38:26,576 --> 00:38:28,786
Paranoia. Are you getting
enough sleep these days?

635
00:38:28,870 --> 00:38:31,623
You know.
I had this weird dream the other day.

636
00:38:31,706 --> 00:38:33,541
-Some woman appeared in it.
-Who?

637
00:38:33,625 --> 00:38:35,209
I woke up before I saw her face.

638
00:38:35,293 --> 00:38:38,546
But you know,
some of it actually made sense.

639
00:38:39,213 --> 00:38:42,383
I was sleeping in a palace courtyard
in the middle of the day.

640
00:38:42,467 --> 00:38:45,011
That would mean I was someone
of some standing, right?

641
00:38:45,094 --> 00:38:48,056
So you're saying
you were a royal in your dream?

642
00:38:48,139 --> 00:38:49,724
Should I buy a lotto ticket?

643
00:38:49,807 --> 00:38:51,726
I feel like it had
some sort of hidden meaning.

644
00:38:51,809 --> 00:38:53,102
No hidden meaning. Just a dream.

645
00:38:53,186 --> 00:38:56,022
Stop chasing women in your dreams
and meet one in real life.

646
00:38:56,105 --> 00:38:58,775
Damn it, why do you always end up there?

647
00:38:58,858 --> 00:39:00,860
You just don't understand yet.

648
00:39:01,361 --> 00:39:02,737
Love is the best medicine.

649
00:39:03,863 --> 00:39:06,574
It's like a powerful shot of oxytocin.

650
00:39:06,658 --> 00:39:07,784
Best medicine, my ass.

651
00:39:08,952 --> 00:39:10,244
You quack.

652
00:39:15,750 --> 00:39:18,044
NEWTUBE
ROYAL CONSORT HUI OF THE KANG CLAN

653
00:39:25,802 --> 00:39:26,970
Okay.

654
00:39:27,053 --> 00:39:28,513
<i>The master of palace intrigue.</i>

655
00:39:28,596 --> 00:39:31,599
<i>How did she get caught up</i>
<i>in all that palace intrigue?</i>

656
00:39:31,683 --> 00:39:32,934
<i>The gangster royal consort.</i>

657
00:39:33,017 --> 00:39:34,644
<i>The truth behind the poison refill.</i>

658
00:39:36,312 --> 00:39:38,815
What do these young punks know?

659
00:39:40,733 --> 00:39:41,776
Damn it.

660
00:39:45,863 --> 00:39:47,490
I should just eat.

661
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:53,287
He still has not learned his lesson yet?

662
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:55,707
Stealing side dishes again?

663
00:39:57,750 --> 00:39:59,127
He deserves to die in his sleep.

664
00:40:00,712 --> 00:40:05,425
Unit 203 is really laying down the law
and asserting her authority.

665
00:40:07,468 --> 00:40:08,636
There's no kimchi either.

666
00:40:16,436 --> 00:40:17,562
Hold on.

667
00:40:18,062 --> 00:40:21,024
Should he not have sent word by now?

668
00:40:24,861 --> 00:40:26,029
Forget it.

669
00:40:26,112 --> 00:40:29,574
That degenerate treats me like I am a spy.
He can die for all I care.

670
00:40:35,747 --> 00:40:36,998
<i>Love is the best medicine.</i>

671
00:40:37,081 --> 00:40:39,417
<i>It's like a powerful shot of oxytocin.</i>

672
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:41,669
Medicine? More like poison.

673
00:40:56,059 --> 00:40:57,268
Cha Se-gye!

674
00:40:59,645 --> 00:41:02,398
Unhand me, you damned brutes!

675
00:41:02,482 --> 00:41:03,816
What are you doing back here?

676
00:41:05,735 --> 00:41:07,320
Damn it.

677
00:41:08,404 --> 00:41:11,282
So, have you considered my proposal?

678
00:41:11,365 --> 00:41:12,617
What proposal?

679
00:41:12,700 --> 00:41:14,952
Oh, that ridiculous proposal
to protect me?

680
00:41:15,036 --> 00:41:15,912
That is right.

681
00:41:16,496 --> 00:41:18,331
I was unaware of your standing then

682
00:41:18,956 --> 00:41:20,917
and acted a bit imprudently.

683
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,502
"A bit"?

684
00:41:22,585 --> 00:41:26,464
Perhaps… more than a bit.

685
00:41:26,547 --> 00:41:28,966
But now that I am fully aware
of your position,

686
00:41:29,467 --> 00:41:32,011
I know your need for my services is
all the more urgent.

687
00:41:32,095 --> 00:41:34,889
You claim to know me so well,
yet you barge in here so arrogantly?

688
00:41:34,972 --> 00:41:36,599
Have you forgotten already?

689
00:41:36,682 --> 00:41:38,810
I am the one who saved your life.

690
00:41:38,893 --> 00:41:40,937
The least you could do
is show eternal gratitude.

691
00:41:41,020 --> 00:41:42,688
You dare forsake your savior?

692
00:41:42,772 --> 00:41:44,190
Oh man. "Savior"?

693
00:41:45,358 --> 00:41:47,527
Stop spouting nonsense
about protecting me

694
00:41:47,610 --> 00:41:49,112
and just ask for money.

695
00:41:49,195 --> 00:41:50,696
The eye is just the mind, looking out.

696
00:41:50,780 --> 00:41:53,991
Perhaps you, who only sees me
as a money-grubber,

697
00:41:54,075 --> 00:41:55,660
are the one possessed by such a spirit.

698
00:41:56,661 --> 00:41:59,413
"Possessed" is a bit much.
Let's go with "CM."

699
00:41:59,497 --> 00:42:00,706
"See-em"?

700
00:42:01,666 --> 00:42:03,626
I have never heard of such a word.

701
00:42:04,127 --> 00:42:05,378
What does it mean?

702
00:42:05,461 --> 00:42:06,504
It means…

703
00:42:09,215 --> 00:42:12,343
Capitalist Monster. "CM."

704
00:42:13,094 --> 00:42:16,389
That is what I am.

705
00:42:17,098 --> 00:42:19,225
-A monster?
-Yeah, a monster.

706
00:42:19,851 --> 00:42:23,437
Simply put, I could easily chew up
and spit out a little greenhorn like you.

707
00:42:24,522 --> 00:42:28,192
So before things get ugly,
you should get out of here.

708
00:42:36,033 --> 00:42:37,076
<i>Why, you little scoundrel!</i>

709
00:42:39,245 --> 00:42:42,748
Ungrateful degenerate. Have you no grace
for those who show you concern?

710
00:42:42,832 --> 00:42:45,293
What do you think you're doing?
Are you insane?

711
00:42:45,376 --> 00:42:46,878
Don't just stand there! Drag her out!

712
00:42:46,961 --> 00:42:48,254
What the--

713
00:42:48,337 --> 00:42:49,839
Stop right there!

714
00:42:49,922 --> 00:42:51,424
Do not flee from me!

715
00:42:51,507 --> 00:42:53,509
Do you think you are invincible?

716
00:42:53,593 --> 00:42:55,887
If you do not value your life,
you will meet an early end!

717
00:42:55,970 --> 00:42:57,680
Assassins do not rest

718
00:42:57,763 --> 00:42:59,807
once a target has eluded them!

719
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:02,101
Damn it.

720
00:43:02,185 --> 00:43:04,645
It is not working.
He is one wicked creature.

721
00:43:05,271 --> 00:43:06,731
As wicked as can be.

722
00:43:09,025 --> 00:43:11,652
Damn it, she's clinging on
like some kind of vengeful ghost.

723
00:43:11,736 --> 00:43:15,323
She's trying to use this fender bender
to change her entire lot in life.

724
00:43:15,406 --> 00:43:17,575
This is all you could get on Shin Seo-ri?

725
00:43:18,409 --> 00:43:20,536
How can someone's life be summed up
in less than a page?

726
00:43:20,620 --> 00:43:23,247
I looked into her further,
but that was all I could find.

727
00:43:23,331 --> 00:43:25,625
She experienced a brief flash
of fame as a child actor,

728
00:43:25,708 --> 00:43:27,543
but no one recognized her
as an adult.

729
00:43:27,627 --> 00:43:29,795
Perpetually stuck
between rookie and nobody, so to speak.

730
00:43:29,879 --> 00:43:32,256
"Nation's Pebble"? Please.
More like a chunk of gravel.

731
00:43:32,340 --> 00:43:34,342
Poor educational background,

732
00:43:34,425 --> 00:43:37,053
a tragic family history,
and a string of part-time jobs…

733
00:43:38,304 --> 00:43:39,388
It all makes sense now.

734
00:43:39,472 --> 00:43:42,225
It does look like that on paper,
but strangely enough, in person,

735
00:43:42,308 --> 00:43:44,602
she doesn't seem like the type
to have any ulterior motive.

736
00:43:44,685 --> 00:43:47,104
She really did seem
genuinely worried about you.

737
00:43:47,188 --> 00:43:50,274
They say it's easier to map the seafloor
than it is to map a person's intentions

738
00:43:50,358 --> 00:43:51,609
for a reason.

739
00:43:51,692 --> 00:43:53,527
Who knows when she'll show up
to cause a scene?

740
00:43:53,611 --> 00:43:55,613
-Keep security as is.
-Yes, sir.

741
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:08,793
He has his subordinate escort me
because he's worried about me,

742
00:44:08,876 --> 00:44:11,045
but to my face,
he treats me like a money-grubber.

743
00:44:11,128 --> 00:44:12,797
And why does he get
so close for no reason?

744
00:44:12,880 --> 00:44:15,800
I have never met someone
so two-faced in my lifetime.

745
00:44:16,467 --> 00:44:18,386
I see. Your first time.

746
00:44:18,469 --> 00:44:21,639
His life is in danger.
How can he remain so carefree?

747
00:44:22,640 --> 00:44:24,600
"Do not wait until it is too late to act."

748
00:44:24,684 --> 00:44:27,353
He will clearly need my help
sooner rather than later.

749
00:44:27,436 --> 00:44:30,606
Yes. I see, Your Majesty.

750
00:44:31,107 --> 00:44:31,983
Well…

751
00:44:32,608 --> 00:44:33,901
I did not say anything earlier

752
00:44:33,985 --> 00:44:36,696
because arguing about etiquette
from 300 years ago would be pointless.

753
00:44:36,779 --> 00:44:39,907
But technically, I am not "Your Majesty."
