<i>I hold on to my grudges,</i>
<i>but I hold on to kindness even tighter.</i>

996
00:56:17,521 --> 00:56:18,814
Have you forgotten already?

997
00:56:18,897 --> 00:56:20,399
I am the one who saved your life.

998
00:56:20,482 --> 00:56:22,401
The least you could do
is show eternal gratitude.

999
00:56:22,484 --> 00:56:23,819
You dare forsake your savior?

1000
00:56:23,902 --> 00:56:25,862
Oh man. "Savior"?

1001
00:56:25,946 --> 00:56:29,241
Unlike some people, I would never treat
my savior like a stray mutt.

1002
00:56:29,324 --> 00:56:30,367
You may rest easy.

1003
00:56:30,450 --> 00:56:32,536
-Who are you talking about?
-Just a scoundrel I know.

1004
00:56:32,619 --> 00:56:34,204
Let us put the past behind us

1005
00:56:34,287 --> 00:56:36,915
and start anew like respectable gentlemen.

1006
00:56:36,999 --> 00:56:38,208
Huzzah!

1007
00:56:39,418 --> 00:56:40,544
Huzzah!

1008
00:56:42,963 --> 00:56:44,423
<i>You miss what's right under your nose.</i>

1009
00:56:44,506 --> 00:56:47,467
I thought it'd blow over quickly,
but that buzz is lasting.

1010
00:56:47,551 --> 00:56:48,885
The marketing team checked,

1011
00:56:48,969 --> 00:56:52,014
and she's been trending at the top
of portal search algorithms for two weeks.

1012
00:56:52,097 --> 00:56:55,225
Turns out that crazy woman wasn't a spy.
She was a hidden gem.

1013
00:56:55,809 --> 00:56:56,852
No point in delaying it.

1014
00:56:56,935 --> 00:56:57,811
Mr. Son.

1015
00:56:58,395 --> 00:57:00,689
You should head out.
We need to claim her first.

1016
00:57:01,398 --> 00:57:03,400
I'm on my way, sir.

1017
00:57:07,571 --> 00:57:09,531
I heard Choi discovered
a new sellout queen?

1018
00:57:09,614 --> 00:57:11,241
I heard she's breaking sales records.

1019
00:57:11,324 --> 00:57:12,951
Her aesthetic is like

1020
00:57:13,035 --> 00:57:14,703
"noblewoman from the Joseon era."

1021
00:57:14,786 --> 00:57:17,247
A kitchen knife lives
or dies by its sharpness.

1022
00:57:17,330 --> 00:57:18,582
Yes, that's right.

1023
00:57:18,665 --> 00:57:20,375
Oh, my. What's going on there?

1024
00:57:25,756 --> 00:57:27,591
A game-changer for the kitchen!

1025
00:57:27,674 --> 00:57:29,843
The undisputed king of the kitchen!

1026
00:57:29,926 --> 00:57:32,471
The emperor of chopping!
The pride of Korean-made knives!

1027
00:57:32,554 --> 00:57:34,306
The Sapphire Rose Knife!

1028
00:57:34,389 --> 00:57:36,808
-And just like that, it's sold out!
-That's right!

1029
00:57:36,892 --> 00:57:39,478
<i>These knife skills, praised even</i>
<i>by the Royal Kitchen</i>

1030
00:57:39,561 --> 00:57:41,521
<i>during my palace maid days,</i>
<i>have not dulled since.</i>

1031
00:57:41,605 --> 00:57:43,815
The Rhythm Chinese Workbook Package.

1032
00:57:43,899 --> 00:57:46,359
This is all you need
to master Chinese in six months.

1033
00:57:46,443 --> 00:57:48,278
"Even the longest journey
begins with one step."

1034
00:57:48,361 --> 00:57:50,530
"No one was ever full
from the first spoonful."

1035
00:57:50,614 --> 00:57:53,158
"One must press forward steadily,
stacking stones one by one."

1036
00:57:53,241 --> 00:57:54,951
That's amazing!

1037
00:57:55,035 --> 00:57:56,369
We're sold out!

1038
00:57:56,453 --> 00:57:58,330
-Sold out!
-Sold out!

1039
00:57:58,413 --> 00:57:59,664
CHINESE WORKBOOK PACKAGE
SOLD OUT

1040
00:57:59,790 --> 00:58:01,750
<i>Mastering the original</i>
Romance of the Three Kingdoms

1041
00:58:01,833 --> 00:58:02,876
<i>has finally paid off.</i>

1042
00:58:02,959 --> 00:58:06,755
A NEW ME, A NEW START
CERONA C

1043
00:58:22,354 --> 00:58:24,523
That is hectopascal-level energy for you.

1044
00:58:24,606 --> 00:58:26,274
You were all surprised, weren't you?

1045
00:58:26,358 --> 00:58:28,693
That is the power packed in every bottle.

1046
00:58:28,777 --> 00:58:32,531
Vitality that makes you do backflips.
You must experience it for yourself.

1047
00:58:32,614 --> 00:58:34,449
Everyone, I'm being told
we're already sold out.

1048
00:58:34,533 --> 00:58:36,910
-We're sold out.
-We sold out!

1049
00:58:36,993 --> 00:58:39,579
-Sold out!
-Sold out!

1050
00:58:39,663 --> 00:58:43,542
<i>When it comes to nimble footwork</i>
<i>and quick reflexes, none can match me.</i>

1051
00:58:44,126 --> 00:58:46,002
-Sold out!
-Sold out!

1052
00:58:46,086 --> 00:58:47,838
ENERGY CERONA C
SOLD OUT

1053
00:58:48,797 --> 00:58:50,966
Where did that woman come from?

1054
00:58:51,049 --> 00:58:53,552
She's just an extra here for the day.

1055
00:58:53,635 --> 00:58:55,929
They've sold through
this quarter's entire allocation.

1056
00:58:56,012 --> 00:58:59,182
The calls are still coming in
even after the sold-out notice.

1057
00:58:59,266 --> 00:59:00,892
Contact the supplier. Get more stock.

1058
00:59:00,976 --> 00:59:03,019
We have to strike while the iron is hot.

1059
00:59:04,187 --> 00:59:06,857
Sir, Ms. Shin isn't picking up her phone.

1060
00:59:07,357 --> 00:59:09,860
She couldn't already be
in talks with someone else, right?

1061
00:59:09,943 --> 00:59:12,487
You need to hurry.
Find the "Nation's Gravel" or whatever.

1062
00:59:12,571 --> 00:59:15,407
We must sign her
before anyone else finds out.

1063
00:59:15,490 --> 00:59:17,909
Get her signature, or it'll be your head.

1064
00:59:19,244 --> 00:59:20,829
Yes, sir.

1065
00:59:32,966 --> 00:59:34,843
It won't take much time.

1066
00:59:34,926 --> 00:59:37,429
You might as well do one more
since you're here anyway.

1067
00:59:37,512 --> 00:59:38,430
Absolutely not.

1068
00:59:38,513 --> 00:59:40,432
It is already past the agreed-upon time.

1069
00:59:40,515 --> 00:59:41,808
I read in the paper

1070
00:59:41,892 --> 00:59:44,978
that overwork is the shortcut
to every ailment known to man.

1071
00:59:46,521 --> 00:59:48,732
Then I'll double your hourly wage.

1072
00:59:48,815 --> 00:59:51,276
Double? We should do it.

1073
00:59:52,152 --> 00:59:54,446
<i>You treated me like some lowly maid</i>
<i>in the beginning.</i>

1074
00:59:54,529 --> 00:59:57,157
<i>It appears you have</i>
<i>finally recognized my worth.</i>

1075
00:59:57,240 --> 00:59:58,158
<i>In that case…</i>

1076
00:59:58,241 --> 00:59:59,659
-Seven times.
-What?

1077
00:59:59,743 --> 01:00:02,370
For seven times the pay,
I shall gladly oblige.

1078
01:00:02,454 --> 01:00:03,455
Wait, what?

1079
01:00:04,497 --> 01:00:06,750
Are you nuts? Don't push it.

1080
01:00:06,833 --> 01:00:09,544
We're not in a gambling den.
Don't try to hit the jackpot here.

1081
01:00:09,628 --> 01:00:12,088
No more, no less. Exactly seven times.

1082
01:00:12,964 --> 01:00:16,384
I mean, come on. Seven times the rate is--

1083
01:00:16,468 --> 01:00:17,969
If you do not like it, look elsewhere.

1084
01:00:18,053 --> 01:00:19,930
Wait. Hold on.

1085
01:00:22,849 --> 01:00:24,517
Deal. Let's do it.

1086
01:00:25,852 --> 01:00:27,729
Wait. That worked?

1087
01:00:29,147 --> 01:00:30,232
Jesus.

1088
01:00:30,774 --> 01:00:32,901
I feel like I've seen her
somewhere before.

1089
01:00:33,526 --> 01:00:34,861
Where was it?

1090
01:00:36,738 --> 01:00:40,700
You can find black goat extract documented
even in the Annals of the Joseon Dynasty.

1091
01:00:40,784 --> 01:00:44,204
They say it was also the secret
to King Anjong's longevity.

1092
01:00:44,287 --> 01:00:46,248
<i>The timing could not be better.</i>

1093
01:00:46,331 --> 01:00:48,375
<i>My vitality has worn considerably thin</i>

1094
01:00:48,458 --> 01:00:50,001
<i>from this compulsory fasting.</i>

1095
01:00:50,085 --> 01:00:52,212
<i>Looks like I will restore</i>
<i>my strength for free.</i>

1096
01:00:52,295 --> 01:00:53,463
You'll probably recognize her.

1097
01:00:53,546 --> 01:00:56,091
She was recently crowned
the mukbang goddess.

1098
01:00:56,174 --> 01:00:59,469
Shall we find out what she thinks
about our black goat extract?

1099
01:00:59,552 --> 01:01:01,805
I'm with the mukbang goddess here.

1100
01:01:01,888 --> 01:01:03,306
This is perfect

1101
01:01:03,390 --> 01:01:06,268
for when you're feeling fatigued
and need an energy boost.

1102
01:01:06,351 --> 01:01:07,394
Here we go.

1103
01:01:09,980 --> 01:01:10,981
Oh, my.

1104
01:01:13,942 --> 01:01:17,988
Medicine that's good for you
often has a bitter aroma.

1105
01:01:18,738 --> 01:01:22,242
At times like this,
it's best to just gulp it down in one go.

1106
01:01:22,325 --> 01:01:23,201
One big gulp.

1107
01:01:23,285 --> 01:01:24,828
<i>Hear me. Bring forth the poison.</i>

1108
01:01:24,911 --> 01:01:26,288
<i>Let go!</i>

1109
01:01:26,371 --> 01:01:27,789
Let go!

1110
01:01:31,668 --> 01:01:33,211
-Take it away!
-Oh no.

1111
01:01:37,632 --> 01:01:41,386
As you can see, taking care
of your health is never easy.

1112
01:01:41,469 --> 01:01:43,221
It requires patience.

1113
01:01:43,305 --> 01:01:45,765
Please don't hang up your calls.

1114
01:01:45,849 --> 01:01:47,267
It tastes perfectly fine.

1115
01:01:47,892 --> 01:01:50,937
Because this is made
with 100% free-range black goat,

1116
01:01:51,021 --> 01:01:52,731
there is nothing to worry about.

1117
01:01:52,814 --> 01:01:54,733
Switch screens!

1118
01:01:57,152 --> 01:01:59,279
You just threw up on live TV.
Are you insane?

1119
01:01:59,362 --> 01:02:01,406
Are you trying to get me fired?

1120
01:02:01,489 --> 01:02:04,451
Do you have any idea what you just did?

1121
01:02:04,534 --> 01:02:05,744
You must know you messed up.

1122
01:02:05,827 --> 01:02:07,954
<i>"Royal Consort Hui of the Kang clan,</i>
<i>of the Inner Court,</i>

1123
01:02:08,038 --> 01:02:09,706
<i>has committed a heinous crime."</i>

1124
01:02:09,789 --> 01:02:10,707
<i>The villainess.</i>

1125
01:02:10,790 --> 01:02:13,585
<i>With a wicked woman</i>
<i>manipulating the throne…</i>

1126
01:02:13,668 --> 01:02:16,296
<i>She was disliked on a cataclysmic level.</i>

1127
01:02:16,379 --> 01:02:17,714
<i>Royal Consort Hui…</i>

1128
01:02:17,797 --> 01:02:19,341
<i>-So loud.</i>
-Don't pretend to be sick.

1129
01:02:19,424 --> 01:02:21,217
-Drop the act.
<i>-Please stop.</i>

1130
01:02:21,301 --> 01:02:23,428
<i>But that commoner's time will soon be up.</i>

1131
01:02:23,511 --> 01:02:26,598
<i>Even the heavens take heed,</i>
<i>now that the wicked vixen is gone.</i>

1132
01:02:31,394 --> 01:02:33,271
I knew you were crazy from the start--

1133
01:02:33,355 --> 01:02:34,731
Shut it!

1134
01:02:34,814 --> 01:02:36,524
Shut that trap of yours!

1135
01:02:37,233 --> 01:02:38,526
My head is pounding.

1136
01:02:38,610 --> 01:02:40,195
"Shut my trap"? You can't be serious.

1137
01:02:40,278 --> 01:02:42,238
You clung to me when you needed me,

1138
01:02:42,906 --> 01:02:45,700
and now that I am no longer useful,
you cast me aside?

1139
01:02:46,326 --> 01:02:48,912
You swallow what is sweet
and spit out what is bitter.

1140
01:02:48,995 --> 01:02:50,705
That is what your despicable trap does!

1141
01:02:50,789 --> 01:02:52,207
You have gone too far, lady.

1142
01:02:52,290 --> 01:02:54,042
You must be insane.

1143
01:02:54,125 --> 01:02:56,294
-How dare you!
-Why, you little…

1144
01:02:57,837 --> 01:02:59,255
Damn it.

1145
01:03:03,093 --> 01:03:04,677
Why, you little…

1146
01:03:11,226 --> 01:03:12,394
Degenerate?

1147
01:03:13,561 --> 01:03:14,729
Found you.

1148
01:03:16,022 --> 01:03:17,148
Shin Seo-ri.

1149
01:03:17,774 --> 01:03:20,235
We must sign her
before anyone else finds out.

1150
01:03:20,318 --> 01:03:22,570
Get her signature, or it'll be your head.

1151
01:03:30,537 --> 01:03:32,288
Found you.

1152
01:03:41,005 --> 01:03:42,048
What are you doing here?

1153
01:03:42,132 --> 01:03:43,967
I came looking for you.

1154
01:03:44,467 --> 01:03:46,219
-Why?
-I have something to tell you.

1155
01:03:46,803 --> 01:03:47,679
Come with me.

1156
01:03:49,806 --> 01:03:52,058
You pop out of nowhere
and tell me to follow you?

1157
01:03:52,142 --> 01:03:55,562
Would it not be a gentleman's duty
to explain the circumstances first?

1158
01:03:55,645 --> 01:03:57,063
A gentleman's duty?

1159
01:04:03,361 --> 01:04:05,405
You know you're really weird, right?

1160
01:04:17,041 --> 01:04:19,043
We can talk about the details later.

1161
01:04:39,564 --> 01:04:40,732
How…

1162
01:04:41,441 --> 01:04:42,358
<i>A kill list?</i>

1163
01:04:43,276 --> 01:04:46,404
It was obtained from an attendant
of His Majesty's quarters.

1164
01:04:49,240 --> 01:04:53,453
ROYAL CONSORT HUI OF THE KANG CLAN

1165
01:04:53,536 --> 01:04:55,705
The one holding a sword to my throat…

1166
01:04:59,334 --> 01:05:00,668
was His Majesty.

1167
01:05:18,686 --> 01:05:20,104
<i>Go in peace.</i>

1168
01:05:27,320 --> 01:05:29,197
-Your Majesty.
-"Your Majesty"?

1169
01:05:35,870 --> 01:05:37,372
Shin Seo-ri.

1170
01:05:45,046 --> 01:05:48,216
What is His Majesty doing here?
Am I seeing things?

1171
01:05:48,299 --> 01:05:52,554
Right. I must have seen an apparition
because I was feeling so dizzy.

1172
01:05:52,637 --> 01:05:54,222
I must gather my wits about me.

1173
01:05:54,305 --> 01:05:55,557
Shin Seo-ri.

1174
01:05:58,560 --> 01:06:00,520
Why would you run away like that?

1175
01:06:00,603 --> 01:06:03,565
Why did you follow me all the way here?

1176
01:06:03,648 --> 01:06:05,149
I said I have something to tell you.

1177
01:06:05,233 --> 01:06:06,192
What?

1178
01:06:06,276 --> 01:06:08,903
Things look serious over there.

1179
01:06:08,987 --> 01:06:10,071
Are they fighting?

1180
01:06:10,154 --> 01:06:11,614
They're clearly not fighting.

1181
01:06:11,698 --> 01:06:13,992
Looks like things are about to heat up.

1182
01:06:14,075 --> 01:06:14,951
Ms. Shin Seo-ri.

1183
01:06:16,202 --> 01:06:17,662
I'd like to offer you a contract.

1184
01:06:17,745 --> 01:06:19,247
A contract?

1185
01:06:19,956 --> 01:06:22,417
You made it clear
I had nothing to offer you.

1186
01:06:22,500 --> 01:06:23,668
No, it turns out you do.

1187
01:06:25,336 --> 01:06:26,754
I need that.

1188
01:06:27,297 --> 01:06:30,300
And in turn, you. Desperately, even.

1189
01:06:31,259 --> 01:06:32,260
You

1190
01:06:32,885 --> 01:06:33,845
need me?

1191
01:06:55,658 --> 01:06:58,494
Here you are.
I've been looking everywhere for you.

1192
01:07:04,042 --> 01:07:04,917
<i>That face…</i>

1193
01:07:07,670 --> 01:07:09,047
<i>He is no apparition.</i>

1194
01:07:13,635 --> 01:07:14,927
What are you doing here?

1195
01:07:22,685 --> 01:07:24,228
Degenerate.

1196
01:07:25,521 --> 01:07:26,981
I am going to need you…

1197
01:07:28,816 --> 01:07:30,526
to be my shield for a moment.

1198
01:08:29,502 --> 01:08:32,797
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

1199
01:08:34,298 --> 01:08:35,425
Help!

1200
01:08:36,092 --> 01:08:37,760
Help me!

1201
01:08:37,844 --> 01:08:39,011
Let me out!

1202
01:08:40,638 --> 01:08:41,848
Let me out of here!

1203
01:08:50,106 --> 01:08:51,315
Help…

1204
01:08:52,525 --> 01:08:53,943
Please let me out.

1205
01:08:54,485 --> 01:08:55,445
Help me.

1206
01:08:55,528 --> 01:08:57,864
YEONGHWI CHAMBER

1207
01:09:11,377 --> 01:09:12,253
Help…

1208
01:09:13,337 --> 01:09:14,589
Please let me out.

1209
01:11:03,781 --> 01:11:05,825
<i>They say cursed ties bind deeper</i>
<i>than destined ones.</i>

1210
01:11:05,908 --> 01:11:07,618
<i>When it feels off, it is best to avoid it.</i>

1211
01:11:07,702 --> 01:11:10,037
<i>It's even more pathetic than I expected.</i>

1212
01:11:10,121 --> 01:11:11,956
Do not tell me you were tailing me.

1213
01:11:12,039 --> 01:11:13,541
<i>Our Se-gye has a woman in his life?</i>

1214
01:11:13,624 --> 01:11:15,585
<i>Just an unknown actress. Nothing special.</i>

1215
01:11:15,668 --> 01:11:18,671
<i>What about the ad campaign?</i>
<i>Can we proceed with Ms. Shin?</i>

1216
01:11:19,630 --> 01:11:21,841
-You were worried about me again.
-Worried? As if.

1217
01:11:21,924 --> 01:11:24,760
<i>Did you dream about a woman you know?</i>
<i>Your first love from a past life?</i>

1218
01:11:24,844 --> 01:11:26,596
<i>"First love"? You've lost your damn mind!</i>

1219
01:11:26,679 --> 01:11:28,848
<i>Let us keep it simple.</i>
<i>We shall just follow our gut.</i>

1220
01:11:28,931 --> 01:11:30,433
<i>What a truly ridiculous woman.</i>

1221
01:11:32,310 --> 01:11:34,312
Subtitle translation by Justin S. Kim

